  "result": "Orders now have a `refunded` state. Paid and shipped orders can move to it, nothing can move out of it, and refunded orders don't count in `sales_by_customer`. The full test suite passes: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` ran 11 tests, all OK.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `shop/orders.py`: added `refunded` to the list of states. `paid` and `shipped` can now move to `refunded`, and `refunded` can't move anywhere.\n- `tests/test_orders.py`: tests that paid\u2192refunded and shipped\u2192refunded work, that every move out of refunded is rejected, and that new\u2192refunded and cancelled\u2192refunded are rejected.\n- `tests/test_reports.py` (new): tests that `sales_by_customer` leaves out refunded orders.\n\n**Didn't need changes:**\n- `shop/reports.py`: `sales_by_customer` only counts orders in a fixed set of states (`paid`, `shipped`), so refunded orders were already left out. `render` builds on it, so the same holds there.\n- `shop/storage.py`: it saves the state as plain text and doesn't check its value.\n- `shop/cli.py` and `README.md` don't mention states at all.\n\nRunning the tests left untracked `__pycache__` directories in the repo. Nothing is committed.",
